      "text": "To determine the cost of the gas used, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the distance driven:**\n   The odometer reading when Ryoysuke picked up his friend was 74,568 miles, and when he dropped his friend off at his house, it read 74,592 miles. The distance driven is:\n   \\[\n   74,592 - 74,568 = 24 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the amount of gasoline used:**\n   Ryosuke's car gets 28 miles per gallon. Therefore, the amount of gasoline used for the 24-mile trip is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{24 \\text{ miles}}{28 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = \\frac{24}{28} = \\frac{6}{7} \\text{ gallons}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the cost of the gasoline:**\n   The price of one gallon of gas is $4.05. Therefore, the cost of the gasoline used is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{6}{7} \\times 4.05 = \\frac{6 \\times 4.05}{7} = \\frac{24.30}{7} \\approx 3.4714\n   \\]\n   Rounding to the nearest cent, the cost is:\n   \\[\n   3.47\n   \\]\n\nThus, the cost of the gas that Ryosuke used to drive his friend back home from work is \\(\\boxed{3.47}\\).",
